V005 ATTEMPT FACTS

The first local output redirection used a misspelled directory name and failed before SSH execution; no remote files changed.

The initial attempt to extract the internal Device ELF .text section with host objcopy failed with "Unable to recognise the format". readelf reported .text file offset 0xb0 and size 0x140dc; dd extracted the text and six functions using those recorded offsets and sizes. The raw error and successful command output are retained in results/device-code-extract-v005.log and results/device-code-extract-v005-retry-01.log.

The first disassembly path contained a repeated results component and exited 1. The corrected path exited 0; llvm-objdump still emitted <not available> for instruction words. Both raw outputs remain in results/device-disassembly-v005.txt and results/device-disassembly-v005-retry-01.txt.

One local artifact identity command used the same misspelled directory component and failed locally. The corrected local/server SHA256 comparison matched for the Candidate source, Runner source, Runner executable, Device ELF/text, and all six function extracts.
